---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import SiteNav from "../../components/SiteNav.astro";
import SiteFooter from "../../components/SiteFooter.astro";
/* Build guide — the bench leaf (Tier 1). Rendered from the repo's
   bench-build-v0.5.md; the repo stays the source of truth (links land at
   A7). Voice: It/I, instructional second-person for the reader. */
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, "");
const repo = "https://github.com/LBM-Labs/Mycelium_Network"; // A7
const parts = [
  ["Raspberry Pi Zero 2 W + 32 GB high-endurance microSD", "$32", "the node's computer"],
  ["Official 5 V 2.5 A micro-USB supply", "$8", "into the PWR IN port"],
  ["Micro-USB OTG adapter", "$3", "into the USB (data) port"],
  ["2-port USB 2.0 hub", "$5", "bus-powered is fine on the 2.5 A supply"],
  ["LILYGO TTGO LoRa32 v2.1 + 915 MHz antenna", "$25", "the radio — never power without the antenna"],
  ["SMA male → SMA female bulkhead cable (RG316, ~20 cm)", "$8", "panel-mounts the antenna"],
  ["EnviroDIY Mayfly v1.1", "$80", "the sensor brain"],
  ["USB-A → USB-C cable (short)", "$4", "hub → Mayfly: power + serial"],
  ["Seeed Grove Temperature Sensor v1.2", "$7", "NTC thermistor, zero wiring"],
  ["Grove cable", "$1", "usually ships with the sensor"],
  ["LED + ~330 Ω resistor + breadboard + 2 jumpers", "$3", "status LED on GPIO 17"],
  ["Plastic project box", "on hand", "it all goes in here"],
];
const topology = `5V 2.5A supply ──► [PWR IN]   (power pins only — no data)

[USB] ── OTG adapter ── 2-port hub ──┬── TTGO LoRa32  → /dev/rnode
                                     └── Mayfly v1.1  → /dev/mayfly

GPIO 17 ── 330 Ω ── LED ── GND       (breadboard)

Mayfly AA0/AA1 Grove socket ── Grove cable ── Grove temp sensor`;
const steps = [
  { h: "Flash the Mayfly", b: "In the Arduino IDE, add the board package <em>EnviroDIY ATmega Boards</em> → <em>EnviroDIY Mayfly 1284P</em> and the <em>Adafruit ADS1X15</em> library. Open the Grove-temp sketch, read its PORT CONFIG header, and upload. With the Grove sensor in the <strong>AA0/AA1 aux-analog socket</strong> (Grove power jumper at 3.3 V), the Serial Monitor at 115200 should show a <code>$MYC,…</code> line every 10 s and the green LED blinking per line — <code>temp_c</code> near your thermostat's opinion." },
  { h: "Set up the Pi", b: "Flash Pi OS Lite 64-bit, clone the repo, run <code>leaf/setup.sh</code>, and do the key + <code>config.toml</code> steps it prints — including <code>sensor = \"mayfly\"</code> in <code>/etc/mycelium-network-leaf/config.toml</code>. Leave <code>gateway_identity_hash</code> blank for now; you'll set it when you build and pair a gateway. Reboot." },
  { h: "Plug the chain together", b: "Wire it per the topology above, then verify both serial devices appear: <code>ls -la /dev/rnode /dev/mayfly</code>. (udev pins each by chip, so hub port order never matters.)" },
  { h: "Start and watch", b: "<code>sudo systemctl start rnsd leaf-node</code>, then <code>journalctl -u leaf-node -f</code>. With no gateway yet, you should see the leaf sampling real readings and queuing them — <code>sampled: temp_c=21.340 (queue depth 1)</code>, the depth climbing — and the LED slow-blinking <em>discovering</em> as it listens for a gateway to announce. That's the leaf working on its own." },
];
---
<Base title="Build guide — the bench leaf" description="Step-by-step: build a Mycelium bench leaf from off-the-shelf parts in an afternoon. A $7 thermometer to an encrypted reading in your own spreadsheet.">
  <SiteNav current="build" />

  <article class="guide" id="main">
    <div class="wrap narrow">
      <p class="crumb mono"><a href={`${base}/build`}>← Build</a> · guide</p>
      <h1>The bench leaf</h1>
      <p class="meta mono">~$176 · an afternoon · no soldering</p>
      <p class="lede">This builds the sensor node itself — the leaf: a Grove
      thermistor → a Mayfly logger → your Pi, which seals each reading with
      AES-256-GCM and hands it to the LoRa radio, queued for delivery, with a
      status LED blinking through it all. USB wall power, no solar, no enclosure.
      A leaf on its own senses, seals, and queues; it starts delivering to a
      spreadsheet you own the moment you <a href={`${base}/build/gateway`}>add a
      gateway</a> — so this guide gets the leaf working and proving itself, no
      gateway required.</p>

      <h2>Parts</h2>
      <table class="parts mono">
        <tbody>
          {parts.map(([p, c, n]) => (
            <tr><td>{p}</td><td class="cost">{c}</td><td class="note">{n}</td></tr>
          ))}
          <tr class="total"><td>Total</td><td class="cost">~$176</td><td></td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <h2>Wiring</h2>
      <p>The Pi Zero 2 W has two micro-USB ports and only one carries data:</p>
      <pre class="evidence mono">{topology}</pre>
      <p class="callout mono">⚠ Never power the radio without its antenna attached
      — transmitting into nothing can kill the TTGO. With the antenna on a
      bulkhead through the box wall, "attached" becomes the box's resting state.</p>
      <p class="dim small">Connector note: LoRa boards are normally standard
      <strong>SMA</strong> (board jack with a centre socket) — not RP-SMA, which
      looks identical in photos and won't mate. Verified June 2026: these boards
      are standard SMA. Order plain SMA.</p>

      <h2>Build steps</h2>
      <ol class="steps">
        {steps.map((s) => (
          <li>
            <h3>{s.h}</h3>
            <p set:html={s.b}></p>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ol>

      <div class="prove">
        <h3>Prove it's real</h3>
        <p>Pinch the thermistor between two fingers for a minute. In the journal,
        the sampled <code>temp_c</code> should climb a few degrees — the whole
        sense-and-seal path, measuring an actual thing. Those queued readings
        start landing in a spreadsheet you own the moment you add a gateway.</p>
      </div>

      <h2>Troubleshooting</h2>
      <ul class="trouble">
        <li><strong>No <code>/dev/mayfly</code>:</strong> run <code>lsusb</code> — if the Mayfly's chip isn't <code>10c4:ea60</code>, adjust the udev rule in <code>leaf/setup.sh</code>.</li>
        <li><strong><code>no valid MSAI line within 45s</code>:</strong> Mayfly unpowered (check the hub), unflashed, or its cable is power-only. Open the port by hand: <code>python3 -m serial.tools.miniterm /dev/mayfly 115200</code>.</li>
        <li><strong>Readings but wrong temperature:</strong> the Grove power jumper is at 5 V while the math assumes 3.3 V — flip the jumper.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>What this proves — and what it doesn't</h2>
      <p><strong>Proves:</strong> the full encrypted pipeline end to end, the
      sensor-protocol contract across two independent implementations, named
      multi-parameter readings, and the whole reliability stack under a real
      sensor.</p>
      <p class="dim"><strong>Doesn't prove:</strong> power architecture,
      weatherproofing, SDI-12, or a submersible water-temp probe — those come
      with the field build and the sonde, once they've survived real weather.</p>

      <div class="ctas">
        <a class="btn-primary" href={`${base}/build/gateway`}>Next: add a gateway →</a>
        <a class="btn-ghost" href={`${base}/build`}>← Back to Build</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>

  <SiteFooter />
</Base>

<style>
  .guide { padding: var(--s-8) 8vw var(--s-7); }
  .crumb { margin-bottom: var(--s-5); }
  .crumb a { color: var(--accent); }
  .guide h1 { margin-bottom: var(--s-2); }
  .meta { color: var(--dim); margin-bottom: var(--s-5); }
  .lede { font-size: clamp(1.05rem, 1.5vw, 1.2rem); color: var(--dim); max-width: 62ch; }
  .guide h2 { margin-top: var(--s-7); font-size: var(--t-h3); }
  .guide p { max-width: 64ch; line-height: 1.7; }
  .guide code { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.86em; color: var(--accent);
    background: var(--bg-raise); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 4px; padding: 1px 5px; }

  .parts { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; margin-top: var(--s-4); font-size: var(--t-small); }
  .parts td { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); padding: var(--s-3) var(--s-3) var(--s-3) 0; vertical-align: top; }
  .parts .cost { color: var(--accent); white-space: nowrap; text-align: right; width: 4.5rem; }
  .parts .note { color: var(--dim); }
  .parts .total td { border-bottom: none; border-top: 1px solid var(--rule); color: var(--ink); padding-top: var(--s-3); }

  .guide .evidence { white-space: pre; }
  .callout { margin: var(--s-5) 0; padding: var(--s-3) var(--s-4); font-size: var(--t-small);
    color: var(--amber); border: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--amber) 35%, transparent);
    border-radius: var(--r-md); background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--amber) 7%, transparent); max-width: 64ch; }

  .steps { list-style: none; counter-reset: step; padding: 0; margin: var(--s-4) 0; }
  .steps li { position: relative; padding: 0 0 var(--s-5) var(--s-7); border-left: 1px solid var(--line); margin-left: 12px; }
  .steps li::before { counter-increment: step; content: counter(step); position: absolute; left: -13px; top: 0;
    width: 26px; height: 26px; border-radius: var(--r-pill); background: var(--bg-raise);
    border: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 45%, transparent); color: var(--accent);
    font: 600 13px/26px var(--font-mono); text-align: center; }
  .steps h3 { margin: 0 0 var(--s-2); font-size: 1.1rem; }
  .steps li:last-child { border-left-color: transparent; }

  .prove { margin: var(--s-6) 0; padding: var(--s-5); border: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 35%, transparent);
    border-radius: var(--r-md); background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 5%, transparent); }
  .prove h3 { margin: 0 0 var(--s-2); color: var(--accent); }

  .trouble { padding-left: var(--s-5); }
  .trouble li { margin-bottom: var(--s-3); line-height: 1.6; max-width: 64ch; }
  .ctas { margin-top: var(--s-7); }
</style>
